==Trivia==
*The Battle Cats Unite! release gap between Japanese and International versions is 5 years, 6 months, and 13 days.
*Since The Battle Cats Unite! Matches the current time with you switch, the player can therefore abuse a bug where you can change the custom time to any day of the week to play any stage no matter the day of the week
*[[Manga Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Cat]]'s addition as the newest Switch-exclusive cat has the widest gap between new content since [[Undies Cat Jr. (Switch Special Cat)|Undies Cat Jr.]] and [[Mallet Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Mallet Cat]], taking 1,248 days between exclusive content.
*Despite claiming over 350 playable characters, there are only 189 units present in the Cat Guide (188 if excluding Catburger). The tagline could simply reference that each form for all units are treated separately.
**In the '''Southeast Asia''' version, only 163 units are obtainable as it does not include any of the units introduced in Patch 1.0.6 onwards.
**In the '''International''' version, only 169 units are obtainable as it does not have the Grandon Mining Corps units and Switch-exclusive Units.
*If the '''Japanese Version''' of the game is launched for the first time without connecting to the internet, UBERFEST ''can'' still be accessible.
**EPICFEST and UBERFEST exclusives (except for [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Gao]]) will not be obtainable; however, the Iron Legion will still be obtainable.
**Advent Stages will also be unplayable without connecting to the internet.
*In the Bandai Namco website for The Battle Cats Unite, there is a subsection listing some of the characters that are obtainable in the game.
** The characters listed are: [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]], [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]], [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|Bird Cat]], [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]], [[Cat Bros (Switch Special Cat)|Cat Bros.]], [[Mallet Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Mallet Cat]], [[Nekondo (Special Cat)|Taekwondo Cat]], [[Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Baozi Cat]], [[Crazed Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Baozi Cat]], [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie]], and [[Li'l Valkyrie Dark (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie Dark]]
*From July 14, 2023, to August 2, 2023, players could unintentionally obtain [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] and [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] units via rolling in the UBERFEST banner. These units were not meant to be available during that time and were patched out in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.7 Update|Patch 1.0.7]]. It was later announced that they would be properly distributed in the future.
**In the September 15, 2023 patch for the JP Version, [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow Gao]] was properly added into the game.
** In the December 15, 2023 patch for the JP Version, [[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Miko Mitama]] and [[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Mitama]] were properly added into the game.
**In the March 15, 2024 patch for the JP Version, [[D'artanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'artanyan]] and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] were properly added into the game.

* [[Kabuto Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kabuto Cat]] and [[Kuwagata Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kuwagata Cat]] are the only Switch-Exclusive Cats to be made free via login bonuses due to a client update.
* When [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Patch 1.0.6]] came out, units who targeted all traits or had a zombie target in the mobile version received it in this update, the only unit to not receive this change was [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]]. This makes its description inaccurate and makes it the only cat in the game to target all traits except for [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies. This makes it an irregularity as units with similar archetypes typically have "target all" except for [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] or [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies.
*[[Evangelist Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Evangelist Cat]] is unlocked when beating the Cats of the Cosmos chapter, predating [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Filibuster Cat X's]] addition and similar unlocking method in the mobile version by almost 2 months.
** Evangelist Cat also has a completely different name in its normal and evolved forms, "Filibuster Cat α" and "Filibuster Cat β" respectively.
* In Patch 1.0.5, [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]] was added to the [[Cat Guide]] but cannot be obtained. It can be speculated that it was for a planned American release, however, with the International release, it may have been a scrapped unit overall.
* The Battle Cats Unite had the volume slider before the mobile version of the game, having it introduced in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.3 Update/JP|Patch 1.0.3]] whereas the mobile version received it in [[Version 12.6 Update|Version 12.6]].
* Enemies that were added in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Patch 1.0.6]] onwards have their enemy trait listed. This is absent in all enemies that were added in the base game.
* This is the only version where the Cat Cannon deals damage on the base, specifically to the opposing player in VS Mode.
*The amount of Cat Food that can be earned from getting treasure dupes ranges from 64,800 Cat Food to 216,000 Cat Food.
*Clearing the entirety of Stories of Legends yields a total 4,800 Cat Food.
*The Battle Cats Unite was featured as trial software for a limited time for Nintendo Switch Online users. It lasted from November 29, 2021 to December 5, 2021. Link to the article is [https://topics.nintendo.co.jp/article/79c15fb9-11c3-4ba3-ac77-948d04c96bf1 here].
**It was shortly put on sale for users who were interested in the game, going from 999 円 to 499 円 from November 29, 2021 to December 12, 2021.

*The digital version of The Battle Cats Unite has had a history of discounts going as low for 499円; but it has also gone for 777円 and 799円 as well.
**Similarly, the International Version has gone on sale for as low as $13.99 instead of its usual $19.99 price tag.
*Just like the mobile version, the Frontline Assault Iron Legion has Might Rekon Corps misspelled on the banner as it says "Mighty Recon Korps."
*The SUPERFEST banner's art is unique to The Battle Cats Unite! as it only contains Gao and Shadow Gao as the only fest units.
**As of December 15, 2023, it now has Miko Mitama and Dark Mitama added to the banner.
**As of March 15, 2024, it now has D'artanyan and D'arktanyan added to the banner.
** Since the Nature's Guardians Elemental Pixies are absent in this version, Nekoluga takes the spot of where Bora sits.
** The text on the banner is also different from the mobile version. In the Switch version it says, "Including All Super Rares!" whereas mobile says, "Including All Uber Rares!"
**The text "Uber Drop Rate UP!!" is absent on the Unite version of the banner.
*Tales of the Nekoluga has some differences compared to its first banner appearance from the mobile version:
**The words "Limited Time Only" are absent on the switch version.
**The words "Pickup Event" are absent on the switch version
**The word "...Right?" is shifted further to the right than it is normally.
* Ancient Heroes Ultra Souls has some graphical differences on the banner:
**The words "Drawn from Japanese myth..." has slightly different placement.
**The Grateful Crane's evolved form is mostly blocked by the logo of the banner.
*The Battle Cats Unite! exceeded 300k downloads on August 1, 2019.
**As of September 2022, PONOS has stated the game reached 1 million copies sold.
**As of December 15, 2025, PONOS has stated the game reached 1.6 million copies sold.
*Sometime around 2023, Bandai Namco discontinued the English prints for the physical copy of The Battle Cats Unite!, making it the rarest Southeast Asia version.
**Korean and Taiwanese versions are still being sold on Bandai's website for retail price, and since they are functionally the same game as the English print, it can be auto-translated into English if someone desires to purchase the game physically for retail price.
*The release gap between launch date and the live patch update for The Battle Cats Unite! for International release was 531 days.

